Sentence 1 says a decision not to carry out a DPIA may be justified if you are confident that the processing is unlikely to result in high risk, and that you should document your reasons. This explains when the decision is justified, not why documenting it matters, such as accountability or the failure it prevents. Sentence 2 only restates the requirement. Neither gives an independent rationale for documenting, and neither mentions the DPO's advice.

Sentence 1 comes closest, since documenting reasons is tied to justifying the decision. That link is only implicit, so I count it as partial.

